And we've made a 10% increase in price from P1 to P3. But notice the difference between Q1 and Q3 and Q4 in Q2 is different even with the same percentage change in price. That's because the elasticity of demand at 2 is greater than the elasticity of demand at 0.5.

21
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:45,960
All this simply means is that when the elasticity of demand increases we can expect bigger percentage change, prices uhh, bigger percentage changes in quantity demand.

