Here we're going to draw our demand curve back in and when we look at the first one we have a perfectly inelastic--we're going to denote this as PI--a perfectly inelastic demand curve. Here the demand curve is vertical. As the price changes there is no change in quantity demand. So we will start at price P1 and we will go to price P2 and quantity demand does not change. Have you ever heard someone say money is no object?

31
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:25,560
They likely exhibit perfectly inelastic demand for a product. We can charge as much or as little as we want and there will be no change with quantity.

