The next one is going to be perfect, uhm is going to be inelastic demand. This one is going to be a demand curve that is relatively steep but not vertical like the perfectly inelastic demand curve. This type of demand curve has an elasticity of demand that is going to be between 0 and 1. Any change in price is met by a less than that percent change in quantity. Meats, vegetables, grains, gas and good friendships are examples here. Next is unit elastic.

33
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:15,880
It has a uniform curve shape throughout. We'll denote this D with a little UE, unit elastic.

34
