We will see a bigger response in quantities demand when prices changes by some amount. Let's say price increase by 2%, then we'd expect quantity to fall by more than 2%. Here the price elasticity is going to be greater than 1 and less than infinity. A lot of household items—like name brand stuff—fall under this category.    Lastly, we have perfectly elastic demand and that is denoted by a horizontal demand curve. This is perfectly

